From: Pixel AOSP maintainers <pixel-aosp@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 00:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Define Frankel-scoped missing feature XML prebuilts

Adevtool replaces stock vendor feature declarations with standard AOSP
prebuilt_etc modules. The Android 17 source tree defines most of those
modules, but omits eight declarations needed by Frankel even though their
Apache-2.0 XML inputs are present in frameworks/native/data/etc.

Undefined PRODUCT_PACKAGES entries do not install anything in the generated
Pixel products. In particular, omitting android.hardware.wifi.aware causes
SystemServer to skip the Wi-Fi Aware service and makes
Context#getSystemService(WifiAwareManager.class) return null to the extracted
Pixel Modem Service.

Define all eight missing modules under Frankel-prefixed Soong names. Explicit
filenames preserve the existing vendor/etc/permissions paths while preventing
the adapter from satisfying unchanged PRODUCT_PACKAGES requests made by Cubs
or future targets. Frankel's reviewed generated-tree sanitizer rewrites only
its eight requests to these scoped names.

This is a project-authored AOSP 17 integration fix.
License: Apache-2.0 (platform/frameworks/native)
---
 data/etc/Android.bp | 56 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 56 insertions(+)

